-- title:
--   Supersingular chart points of the special fibre are crossing points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \geq 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1} \cdot jNumQ$ under coefficientwise base change, assumed nonzero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$. Let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $i_1, i_2$ be closed immersions over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ from $C_1$, $C_2$ into the base change along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ of the two-chart model morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), i.e. morphisms $\varphi$ with $\varphi$ followed by the base-changed structure morphism equal to $c_i$; assume every point of that pullback lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$. Let $x$ be a point of the pullback and $y$ a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) of $K$, such that the image of $y$ under [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) equals the image of $x$ under the first projection, and $p \in y$. Assume finally that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from that chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel exactly $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is: every Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ that is elliptic and has $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. The conclusion is that $x$ lies in the intersection of the images of $i_1$ and $i_2$ on underlying spaces.
--
--   This is the implication 'supersingular $\Rightarrow$ crossing point' for the reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$: a geometric point of the special fibre of the two-chart model lying over a supersingular point of the finite $j$-chart belongs to both of the two given components, as in the Deligne–Rapoport description of the fibre as two copies of $X_1(M)$ crossing at the supersingular points. It is used in the corresponding statement about the Hecke degeneracy morphism on components of the special fibre.
